EXCEPTION — OPEN SOURCE COMPONENTS

The following packages are distributed separately under the Apache License,
Version 2.0, and are NOT covered by the proprietary terms above. Each carries
its own LICENSE file, which governs that package:

    packages/sdk         @intyga/sdk
    packages/verify      @intyga/verify
    packages/sdk-go      github.com/intyga-dev/sdk-go
    packages/sdk-rust    intyga-sdk (crates.io)
    packages/sdk-python  intyga-sdk (PyPI)
    packages/verify-go   github.com/intyga-dev/verify-go
    packages/verify-rust intyga-verify (crates.io)
    packages/mcp-sdk     @intyga/mcp-sdk
    packages/mcp-proxy   @intyga/mcp-proxy
    packages/config      @intyga/config

The intyga-verify Python package (assembled from scripts/templates/verify-python
plus verifier modules extracted from packages/sdk-python) is likewise Apache-2.0.

These are the packages published to the public intyga-dev repositories by
.github/workflows/sync-public-packages.yml and sync-public-mcp.yml. Customers
integrating with Intyga need them to verify approval receipts offline, which is
why they are permissively licensed: an independent verifier that nobody may
lawfully run would defeat the purpose of an offline witness guarantee.

